<https://www.synapse.org/#!Synapse:syn26004582>
        :studyStatus                "Completed" ;
        :diseaseFocus               :Neurofibromatosis_Type_1 ;
        :studyName                  "Gene Network Guided Drug Combination in Plexiform Neurofibromas" ;
        :initiative                 "2021 Hack for Rare" ;
        rdf:type                    :Hackie ;
        :grantDOI                   <https://www.doi.org/10.7303/syn26004582> ;
        :fundingAgency              "CTF" ;
        :studyLeads                 "3430741" ;
        :studyLeads                 "3332479" ;
        :description                "Plexiform neurofibromas (PN) are congenital tumors initiated by the loss of function of the Nf1 gene in children and young people. PN cell lines-based drug screen serves as an efficient way to identify the potential drug candidates. However, NF1-associated tumors easily develop drug resistance and relapse after treatment withdrawal. Drug combination may benefit the patients significantly by enhancing the inhibitory effects, reducing the single drug-related side effects." ;
        :acknowledgementStatements  "If you use data/concepts from this hackathon project in a publication or talk, please acknowledge the authors of this hackathon project. In addition, please acknowledge the Children's Tumor Foundation and NF Data Portal using the following statement: \"The results published here are in whole or in part based on data/concepts made available through the NF Open Science Initiative and CTF Hack for Rare 2021.\"" .

<https://www.synapse.org/#!Synapse:syn26008052>
        :studyName                  "LetstalkaboutNF.com -- curated podcast series that facilitates discussion around the shared yet unique experiences of the NF community" ;
        :acknowledgementStatements  "If you use data/concepts from this hackathon project in a publication or talk, please acknowledge the authors of this hackathon project. In addition, please acknowledge the Children's Tumor Foundation and NF Data Portal using the following statement: \"The results published here are in whole or in part based on data/concepts made available through the NF Open Science Initiative and CTF Hack for Rare 2021.\"" ;
        :fundingAgency              "CTF" ;
        :initiative                 "2021 Hack for Rare" ;
        :grantDOI                   <https://www.doi.org/10.7303/syn26008052> ;
        :description                "Patients grapple with a myriad of personal and social issues throughout their life. Furthermore, with NF being a rare disease, many stakeholders have difficulty finding others with shared experiences, connecting with them, and hearing their stories.As part of our project, we have developed a website, which houses a curated podcast series on which we convene patients, caregivers, and clinicians to discuss the topics that matter most to the NF community." ;
        :studyLeads                 "3428700" ;
        rdf:type                    :Hackie ;
        :studyLeads                 "3418671" ;
        :studyStatus                "Completed" ;
        :studyLeads                 "3431386" .

<https://www.synapse.org/#!Synapse:syn26010238>
        :acknowledgementStatements  "If you use data/concepts from this hackathon project in a publication or talk, please acknowledge the authors of this hackathon project. In addition, please acknowledge the Children's Tumor Foundation and NF Data Portal using the following statement: \"The results published here are in whole or in part based on data/concepts made available through the NF Open Science Initiative and CTF Hack for Rare 2021.\"" ;
        rdf:type                    :Hackie ;
        :fundingAgency              "CTF" ;
        :studyStatus                "Completed" ;
        :studyLeads                 "3428910" ;
        :description                "Our solution is to create totally synthetic and customizable full-body MRI images. During the acceleration we would like to train customized models with the following features and parameters: tumors (Number, Size, Location), Patient (Sex, Age), MRI (Modality, Slice thickness, Slice number, Noise level, Comorbidities, Intensity non-uniformity)." ;
        :initiative                 "2021 Hack for Rare" ;
        :diseaseFocus               :Neurofibromatosis_Type_1 ;
        :studyLeads                 "3428911" ;
        :grantDOI                   <https://www.doi.org/10.7303/syn26010238> ;
        :studyName                  "Synthetic NF1 MRI Images" .

